      "writtenOn": "2022-06-30T07:19:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m looking for a generic name too. I checked USB Type-C cable spec R2.1 which is latest, in Table 6-3 \"USB4 cable identity summary\", LRD is listed as name of the cable which has ID header VDO active but TBT3 Discover mode VDO is active; in Figure 5-1 the flow has \"TBT3 LRD active\", that is asking if TBT3 Discover Mode VDO bit 25 is active. I couldn\u0027t find a formal name used by USB spec. If \"LRD\" is too specific, how about call this \"passive with TBT3 active cable\"?  tbt_is_passive_with_tbt3_active_cable()? or just \"TBT3 active cable?",
      "parentUuid": "193cbff9_df9b045d",
